    goal: ['I can understand a short travel update and confirm the help being offered.', '旅行中の短い連絡を聞き、提案されている対応を確認できる。'],
    intro: ['Emma and Ren arrive in Seoul late in the evening. Their hotel has received a booking for only one room instead of two. Emma asks the receptionist to check alternatives. The room problem is resolved, but in the morning they discover that their presentation adapter is missing. They need help again, and the meeting is getting closer.', 'エマとレンは夜遅くソウルに到着します。ホテルには二部屋ではなく一部屋だけの予約が届いていました。エマが受付に別の方法を確認します。部屋の問題は解決しますが、翌朝、発表用の変換アダプターがないと気付きます。会議の時間が迫る中、また助けが必要になります。'],
    warmup: 'Which details would you confirm when someone offers help with a hotel problem?',
    words: [['There is an error in our reservation.', 'reservation', '予約に間違いがあります。'], ['Would it be possible to check another hotel?', 'Would it be possible to', '別のホテルを確認していただくことは可能ですか。'], ['The hotel will cover the difference.', 'cover the difference', 'ホテルが差額を負担します。'], ['We need an adapter for the laptop.', 'adapter', 'ノートパソコン用の変換アダプターが必要です。'], ['Could we borrow one?', 'borrow', '一つお借りできますか。'], ['Please return it after the meeting.', 'return', '会議の後に返してください。']],
    discussion: ['II. You are Emma. Your tutor is a receptionist. Explain a booking problem and politely ask for help.', 'あなたはエマ役、講師は受付係役です。予約の問題を説明し、丁寧に助けを求めましょう。'], followup: 'Which cost or location detail should you confirm before accepting?',
    tips: [
      { rule: ['Listen for the problem, the offered solution, and any cost. Words such as instead and cover can change what you need to do or pay.', '問題、提案された対応、費用を聞き取りましょう。instead や cover などの言葉で、必要な行動や支払いが変わることがあります。'], examples: [['Only one room is available here. A second room is at our partner hotel.', 'こちらには一部屋しか空いていません。もう一部屋は提携ホテルにあります。'], ['We will cover the extra cost.', '追加費用はこちらで負担します。']] },
      { rule: ['Use Would it be possible to ...? or Could we ...? to request assistance. Confirm where, when and how to return a borrowed item.', 'Would it be possible to ...? や Could we ...? で対応を依頼できます。借りた物は、返却する場所や時間、方法も確認しましょう。'], examples: [['Could we borrow an adapter?', '変換アダプターをお借りできますか。'], ['So we should collect it at reception at eight?', 'では、8時に受付で受け取ればよいのですね。']] },
    ],
    apply: { situation: ['Listen to the receptionist\'s update about the two rooms. Identify the location, extra cost and next action.', '二部屋についての受付係の連絡を聞きましょう。場所、追加費用、次にすることを聞き取りましょう。'], text: '<p>I am sorry about the booking error. We have only one room here tonight. Our partner hotel, five minutes away on foot, has a second room. We will cover the extra room cost. You can choose who stays where. Please collect both confirmation slips at this desk. Tomorrow, meet here at eight before you leave for the client\'s office.</p>', questions: [['What is the update about?', 'A solution to the room booking error.'], ['Where is the second room?', 'At the partner hotel, five minutes away on foot.'], ['Who pays the extra room cost?', 'The hotel.'], ['What should they collect?', 'Both confirmation slips at this desk.']] },
    choose: [['Would it be possible (to check / checking) the booking?', 'to check'], ['Could we (borrow / borrowed) an adapter?', 'borrow'], ['The hotel will (cover / covers) the extra cost.', 'cover'], ['The second room is five minutes (away / ago).', 'away'], ['Please return it (after / while) the meeting.', 'after'], ['We should meet (at / on) eight.', 'at']],
    choices: [['The receptionist says the hotel will cover the extra cost. What does that mean?', 'Emma must pay twice.', 'The hotel will pay the additional amount.', 'B'], ['The second room is at a partner hotel. Where should they collect the slips?', 'At this reception desk.', 'At the airport.', 'A'], ['You need an adapter temporarily. Which request fits?', 'Could we keep every laptop forever?', 'Could we borrow an adapter?', 'B'], ['The receptionist gives collection and return instructions. What helps?', 'Repeat the key details to confirm them.', 'Assume the return time is unimportant.', 'A']],
    mission: { situation: ['You are Emma on the morning of the client meeting. Your tutor is Ren. Listen to the receptionist\'s new message about an adapter, then explain the arrangement to Ren.', 'あなたは依頼主との会議の朝のエマ役、講師はレン役です。変換アダプターについての受付係の新しい伝言を聞き、レンに手配を伝えましょう。'], task: ['Confirm what you can borrow, where and when to collect it, when to test it, and how to return it. Ask for clarification if needed, then agree who will collect it.', '借りられる物、受け取る場所と時間、動作確認の時間、返却方法を確認しましょう。必要なら聞き直し、誰が受け取るか決めましょう。'], roles: ['Ren', 'Emma'], text: '<p>Good morning, Emma. We found an adapter you can borrow free of charge. Collect it from this reception desk at eight. Please test it with your laptop here before leaving. Your taxi is booked for eight thirty. Return the adapter to this desk after your meeting, before six this evening. If it does not work, tell us immediately so we can call the client.</p>', lines: ['Emma, what did reception say about the adapter?', 'Is there a charge, and where do we collect it?', 'Should we test it here or wait until the presentation?', 'When is our taxi booked?', 'What should we do if the adapter does not work?', 'I can check the presentation file while you collect it. Does that work?', 'And what is the return deadline?'], evidence: 'Adapter loan free; same reception desk8am; test with laptop before leaving; taxi8:30; report failure immediately so staff can call client; return same desk aftermeeting before6pm. Agree collector/checker. Do not confuse last night\'s second-room location with the adapter desk or invent a purchase.', useful: ['The receptionist said ...', 'We can borrow ... free of charge.', 'We should collect it at ...', 'We need to test it before ...', 'If it does not work, ...', 'We must return it before ...'] },
    topics: [['ASKING FOR HELP', ['How can you explain a problem briefly?', 'What makes a request polite?', 'When should you ask someone to repeat a detail?']], ['TRAVEL CHECKS', ['What equipment belongs on a travel checklist?', 'Which details should you keep offline?', 'How can you check a booking together?']], ['BORROWING', ['What should you confirm before borrowing something?', 'Why is testing it useful?', 'How can you make sure it is returned?']]],
    trivia: ['"Borrow" describes receiving something temporarily; "lend" describes giving it temporarily. Emma borrows an adapter from the hotel. The hotel lends the same adapter to Emma. The object and arrangement are the same, but the point of view changes.', 'borrow は一時的に借りること、lend は一時的に貸すことです。エマはホテルからアダプターを borrow し、ホテルはエマに同じ物を lend します。物も手配も同じですが、立場が変わります。'], triviaQuestion: ['Does the hotel borrow or lend the adapter to Emma?', 'It lends the adapter to Emma.'],
