    discussion: ['II. You are Emma. Your tutor is Ren. Discuss one attractive part of an overseas assignment and one detail to confirm.', 'あなたはエマ役、講師はレン役です。海外勤務の魅力と、確認したい点を一つずつ話しましょう。'], followup: 'What would you need in writing before making a decision?',
    tips: [
      { rule: ['Read status words carefully. Selected confirms a decision; proposed and to be confirmed identify details that are still open.', '状況を示す言葉に注意して読みましょう。selected は決定を示し、proposed や to be confirmed はまだ確定していない点を示します。'], examples: [['Our agency has been selected for the project.', '私たちの会社はその案件に選ばれました。'], ['The start date is proposed, not confirmed.', '開始日は提案されたもので、確定ではありません。']] },
      { rule: ['Use have been offered for an opportunity received, and If we accept, we will ... for a possible consequence. Check an updated document before deciding.', 'have been offered で受けた提案を、If we accept, we will ... で受けた場合の見通しを伝えられます。決める前に最新の書類を確認しましょう。'], examples: [['We have been offered a three-month assignment.', '3か月の現地勤務を提案されています。'], ['If we accept, we will work in Seoul for three months.', '受ければ、ソウルで3か月働くことになります。']] },
    ],
    apply: { situation: ['Read the agency manager\'s message after the client decision. Identify what has been won and what still needs agreement.', '依頼主の決定後の上司からの連絡を読みましょう。何が決定し、何に合意が必要か確認しましょう。'], text: '<h3>Client decision - Seoul project</h3><p>Congratulations, Emma and Ren. Our agency has been selected. The client liked your clear concept and practical technical plan.</p><p>The client has also offered you a three-month assignment in Seoul. A start four weeks from today has been proposed. This is not a confirmed start date.</p><p>Accommodation, travel costs and the return arrangement still need written agreement. Do not book the longer stay yet. Your current presentation trip ends as planned tomorrow.</p><p>Please send your questions by Friday at 3 p.m. We will request a written assignment offer before either of you accepts.</p>', questions: [['Has the agency won the project?', 'Yes. It has been selected.'], ['How long is the proposed assignment?', 'Three months.'], ['Is the start date confirmed?', 'No. A start in four weeks is only proposed.'], ['What should Emma and Ren do by Friday at three?', 'Send their questions.']] },
    choose: [['We have been (offered / offer) an assignment.', 'offered'], ['If we (accept / accepted), we will work in Seoul.', 'accept'], ['The project decision (is / are) confirmed.', 'is'], ['We are considering (accepting / accept).', 'accepting'], ['Please send questions (by / since) Friday.', 'by'], ['The proposed date has not been (confirmed / confirm).', 'confirmed']],
    choices: [['The manager says the agency has been selected. What is confirmed?', 'The agency won the project.', 'Every travel detail is final.', 'A'], ['Which action follows the first message?', 'Book three months of accommodation immediately.', 'Send questions and wait for the written offer.', 'B'], ['A start in four weeks is proposed. What does proposed mean?', 'Suggested but not yet agreed.', 'Already completed.', 'A'], ['Which sentence keeps the offer and acceptance distinct?', 'Receiving an offer means we have accepted it.', 'We have an offer, but we still need to decide.', 'B']],
    mission: { situation: ['You are Emma. Your tutor is Ren. A week later, you receive the new written assignment terms below. Read them before deciding whether to accept together.', 'あなたはエマ役、講師はレン役です。一週間後、次の新しい現地勤務条件が書面で届きます。一緒に受けるか決める前に読みましょう。'], task: ['Explain what has changed since the first message. Confirm dates, accommodation, costs and the return plan. Decide whether to accept the written terms and say how you will reply.', '最初の連絡から変わった点を説明しましょう。日程、滞在先、費用、帰国後の予定を確認し、書面の条件を受けるか決め、返答方法を伝えましょう。'], roles: ['Ren', 'Emma'], title: 'Written assignment terms', text: '<h3>Written assignment terms - updated offer</h3><p>Duration: three calendar months, starting three weeks from today. This replaces the earlier proposed start in four weeks from the first message.</p><p>The agency will book and pay for separate furnished apartments and return economy flights. Keep receipts for approved local work travel; it will be reimbursed.</p><p>Emma leads the creative work. Ren leads technical delivery. After the assignment, both return to their existing Japan-based roles.</p><p>Reply by Tuesday at noon. Acceptance is required before bookings are made. The project award is already confirmed; this document concerns the temporary assignment.</p>', lines: ['Emma, what does the updated offer confirm?', 'Is the timing consistent with the first message?', 'Who pays for the apartments and return flights?', 'What about local work travel, and what do we need to keep?', 'Would we be leaving our Japan-based jobs permanently?', 'These written terms work for me. What do you think?', 'How shall we reply before the deadline?'], evidence: 'Fresh terms received1weeklater: start3weeksfromnow equals4weeksfromfirstmessage, now writtenconfirmed offer; 3calendar months; separate furnished apartments and return economy flights booked/paidagency afteracceptance; approved localworktravel reimbursed keepreceipts; Emma creative Ren technical; returnexistingJapanroles; replyTue noon. Require an explicit acceptance/clarification decision and response, no invented permanent move or self-funded housing. Canonical closing follows acceptance.', useful: ['The updated offer confirms ...', 'Unlike the first message, ...', 'The agency will cover ...', 'We need to keep ...', 'If we accept, ...', 'Let\'s reply by ...'] },
    topics: [['READING OFFERS', ['Which details belong in writing?', 'How can you track changes between versions?', 'Why does a reply deadline matter?']], ['WORKING ABROAD', ['What support would help during a temporary assignment?', 'What would you ask about housing?', 'How would you stay in touch with your team?']], ['DECIDING TOGETHER', ['Which terms should both people check?', 'How can you express a concern politely?', 'What makes an acceptance clear?']]],
    trivia: ['"Cover" and "reimburse" describe different payment arrangements. If an agency books and pays for a flight, it covers the cost directly. If you pay an approved fare first and later receive the money back, it reimburses you. Both reduce your final expense, but the timing differs.', 'cover と reimburse は支払いの仕組みが違います。会社が航空券を予約して直接払うなら、費用を cover します。承認された運賃を自分で払い、後で返してもらうなら reimburse されます。最終的な負担は減りますが、支払いの時期が違います。'], triviaQuestion: ['If Emma pays an approved work fare first and gets it back later, which word fits?', 'Reimburse.'],
    closing: 'The agency wins the project. After a week of checking written terms, Emma and Ren accept a temporary three-month Seoul assignment beginning in three weeks. The agency will arrange housing and return flights; they will return to their Japan-based roles afterward.',
