    mission: { situation: ['You are Emma at the farewell dinner. Your tutor is Claire. Read the new dinner note below, then respond to the plans and reflect on your time at Kamo House.', 'あなたは送別の夕食にいるエマ役、講師はクレア役です。次の新しいメモを読み、予定への返事とKamo Houseでの振り返りを伝えましょう。'], task: ['Thank two friends for specific contributions. Explain one thing you have learned. Confirm the first call and update plan, and distinguish Leo\'s upcoming opening from a bakery already open.', '二人の友達に具体的なことへの感謝を伝え、学んだことを一つ話しましょう。最初の通話と近況連絡の予定を確認し、レオの開店はこれからだとはっきりさせましょう。'], roles: ['Claire', 'Emma'], title: 'Tonight and the next three months', text: '<h3>Farewell dinner - Claire\'s new note</h3><p>Leo has prepared dinner. Riverbend Bakery is still being fitted out; its opening date is not yet confirmed. He will send photos when it is ready.</p><p>Nao has made Emma a travel cup and is preparing pieces for her upcoming Fukuoka exhibition. Claire has finished the photo album.</p><p>Emma and Ren have accepted the three-month Seoul assignment and will return to their Japan-based roles afterward.</p><p>First group video call: the first Sunday after arrival, at 8 p.m. in Kyoto. Ren will send the invitation link. Please confirm you can join. Use the group chat for small updates between calls; later call dates will be agreed separately.</p>', lines: ['Emma, what would you like to say to everyone tonight?', 'Which two contributions would you like to thank people for?', 'What have you learned since your first day here?', 'Is Leo\'s bakery already open, or are we waiting for an update?', 'When is our first group call, and who sends the link?', 'How can we share news between calls?', 'We will miss you. What are you looking forward to when you return?'], evidence: 'Freshnote: Leo dinner and bakeryfitoutnotopen/dateunconfirmed; Nao cup/upcomingFukuokaexhibition; Claire album; accepted3monthassignment then Japanroles. Thanks2specificcontributions; reflection tied tostory. FirstSundayafterarrival8pmKyoto, Renlink, confirmattendance; groupchatbetween, laterdatesnotfixed. Do not invent permanentemigration, completedexhibition, openedbakery or fixedweeklycall. Reconciliation acknowledgespast without demanding restoredromance.', useful: ['Looking back, ...', 'I am grateful for ...', 'Thank you for ...', 'I have learned to ...', 'The opening is still ...', 'So our first call is ...'] },
